  "correct": "D",
  "explanation": "DimDate plays two roles here. USERELATIONSHIP turns on the inactive relationship for this one calculation, and because only one relationship between two tables can be active at a time, the arrival relationship is ignored while it runs. The date filter lands on DepartureDate, and every other measure keeps using arrival date.",
